    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493310038/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """- a confoundedly silly woman who only looks at things to talk about them afterwards in America. Alice came full of flame and fury at the discomforts of her Pension, and raved she would not stay there another day.
Called on Christina, and then on Miss Erichsen, at Mrs. Ross’. Miss Erichsen has had a “change of heart”, and is as if converted, only  to nothing.
Saturday Dec. 6. 1902.
Mrs. Gardner’s £11,000 for the Dürer arrived, also £1,000 for an ivory Madonna Costantini has. 
Alice and Zangwill came to tea, he very bearish and self-absorbed, she in a bitter temper and decided to stay and make the best of it and learn Italian. Bene."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 109 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1902-03> .

